From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:38:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Install where the target interpreter installs

Install schemes, site-packages, the user site and whether it is enabled,
virtual environment detection, EXTERNALLY-MANAGED, which distributions
are local, the uninstall guards and the site configuration file now come
from the target interpreter rather than from this process's sys, site and
sysconfig. For kpip's own interpreter the code paths are pip's, unchanged;
another Python is asked through its preferred schemes, which every Python
kpip installs for has. The default --src directory is found when used,
since which Python a command installs for is not known before it starts.
